        "line": 29,
        "text": "Family 014 retains the four characteristic conditions, its two distinct geometric regimes, the specified rational action, and the conditional primed rational trace comparison. Tensor/fusion compatibility and rational orbit projectors already exist. The finite-level global section constructs commuting normal operators and a finite reduced rational good-place image, with Galois-fixed orbit idempotents; it does not count their ranks. The Arthur enhancement is conditional on an occurring excursion character and gives an identity on the whole Weil group in the full possibly disconnected centralizer. It does not classify packets. Unramified genericity and globally generic exceptional-group every-place temperedness have different hypotheses. The latter applies to G2,F4,E6,E7,E8, split connected adjoint absolutely simple function-field groups, without a depth/characteristic exclusion. Weak containment gives ||R(f)||<=||lambda_v(f)||; summing diagonal matrix elements gives |tr R(f)|<=dim(H_m)||lambda_v(f)|| on the stated finite cuspidal space. No residual/continuous-spectrum or level-saving assertion is added. This preserves the original verdict; it is not a fresh truth audit of these stipulated operations."
